# WordPress AI Client

Ahentic uses WordPress’s official **AI Building Blocks** for model access. Prefer Core / official packages over custom HTTP clients or vendor SDKs.

## Reference docs

- [Introducing the AI Client in WordPress 7.0](https://make.wordpress.org/core/2026/03/24/introducing-the-ai-client-in-wordpress-7-0/)
- [WordPress/php-ai-client](https://github.com/WordPress/php-ai-client) (underlying provider-agnostic PHP SDK)
- [Using Abilities To Build AI in WordPress](https://j.cv/using-abilities-to-build-ai-in-wordpress/) (patterns: single-shot, agent loops, workflows)

## Prefer Core when available

On WordPress **7.0+**, prefer the built-in AI Client entry point:

```php
$text = wp_ai_client_prompt( 'Summarize the benefits of caching in WordPress.' )
	->using_temperature( 0.7 )
	->generate_text();

if ( is_wp_error( $text ) ) {
	// Handle missing provider / generation failure.
	return;
}
```

Key ideas from Core:

- Describe *what* you need; WordPress routes to a site-configured provider/model.
- Use `using_model_preference( ... )` for soft preferences — never hard-require a vendor.
- Prefer `generate_*_result()` when you need token usage / provider / model metadata.
- Feature-detect: sites may have no AI provider configured (**Settings → Connectors**).
- Always handle `WP_Error` from generation methods.

## Fallback / Composer SDK

When Core helpers are unavailable (or for lower-level control), use **`wordpress/php-ai-client`**:

```bash
composer require wordpress/php-ai-client
```

```php
use WordPress\AiClient\AiClient;

$text = AiClient::prompt( 'Write a short summary.' )->generateText();
```

- Bundle via Composer (SDK, not a plugin).
- Prefer this over OpenAI/Anthropic/Google SDKs directly.
- Do not add alternate PHP AI client libraries unless php-ai-client / Core cannot cover the need — document why.

## Usage in Ahentic

- Server-side generation, embeddings, and provider selection go through Core AI Client and/or php-ai-client.
- Keep provider details behind these APIs so models stay swappable per site.
- Pair AI generation with the **Abilities API** for tool/action execution (see abilities rule) — do not invent parallel ad-hoc tool registries when Abilities fit.
- UI (React sidebar) should not call vendors directly; talk to WordPress (REST / abilities / our PHP layer).
